{
  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "The strongest finding so far is the massive multiprofile gain: config_048 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted) reached 0.706 vs config_036 (same but singleprofile) at 0.537, a +0.169 jump. However, it is unclear whether this gain is driven by multiple RNA profiles, multiple image profiles, or the interaction. In the singleprofile setting, the image contributed only ~0.017 (config_036 vs config_049). Config_035 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean ablation that removes the image modality while preserving the multiprofile RNA pipeline and avgpool aggregation. If config_035 approaches ~0.70, the image adds little in the multiprofile regime and future effort should focus on RNA aggregation/fusion. If it drops substantially (e.g., below 0.60), the image profiles are a critical contributor and we should prioritize image-side design choices (aggregation, encoder). This single experiment isolates the image's marginal contribution in the multiprofile setting—the most important open question given the limited budget—without changing multiple variables simultaneously."
}

